! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: trainers cannot confidently distinguish required participation from optional participation.

  + context: Minted by library-loop problem-authoring batch A5 from the committed UKRN training manuscript.
  + IF:
    Trainers must decide how to participate in and reproduce a programme locally.
  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the independent committed source: “It wasn't very clear to us how many sessions we needed to have attended, which ones were fundamental … and which ones then were optional.” (source: futon5a essays/ukrn-open-research-training-plos-one/ukrn-open-research-training-plos-one-v2.5-submission.md:146)
  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer the fixed/flexible specification problem.
  + BECAUSE:
    The source records uncertainty before the library patterns prescribe a scaffold.
